[{"_1":2},"llms/mdx",{"_3":4},"data","# IoT Fleets (/docs/platform/iot-fleets/overview)\n\n\n\nIoT Fleets applies PKI to the device lifecycle: registration, obtaining an identity, renewal and retirement. It is intended for those who administer a device population and those who integrate its enrollment client or the system that accepts it.\n\nStart here [#start-here]\n\nFollow [Enroll and connect your first device](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device) to prepare a DMS, obtain the identity from the client and demonstrate an mTLS connection. The automatic path includes initial trust, a CSR and result checks.\n\nTo start with an existing certificate, use [Register a device manually](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device). You can then prepare enrollment and renewal for the next device.\n\nDevices and identities [#devices-and-identities]\n\n| Resource     | What it represents                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Device**   | An inventory entry with an identifier, owning DMS and classification.              |\n| **Identity** | The device's association with its certificates: an active version and a history.   |\n| **DMS**      | The service that configures admission, enrollment, renewal and trust distribution. |\n| **Fleet**    | The population you operate, represented through devices, DMSs, tags and metadata.  |\n\nEach device has an owning DMS. You can organize a population through several DMSs when it needs different policies, and use tags to classify it. “Fleet” describes that operational context; the resources you create and query are DMSs and devices.\n\n[Device management](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/device-management) covers states, certificate history and identity actions. During renewal, retain the relationship with the device and check which certificate becomes the current identity.\n\nEnrollment with PKI [#enrollment-with-pki]\n\nThis section connects PKI rules to the device client. Preparation follows this order:\n\n1. **CA and profile:** prepare the issuer and certificate rules in [PKI](/docs/platform/pki/overview).\n2. **DMS policy:** define how the device is admitted, how requests authenticate and which trust is distributed.\n3. **Client:** prepare the initial credential, server trust, and key generation or custody.\n4. **Result:** request the certificate, install it and check its association with the device.\n5. **Continuity:** configure renewal, successor installation and recovery according to DMS policy.\n\n<Cards>\n  <Card title=\"Configure the DMS\" description=\"Prepare the CA, admission, authentication and renewal rules.\" href=\"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/dms\" />\n\n  <Card title=\"Integrate the EST client\" description=\"Review the device endpoints, formats and checks.\" href=\"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/est-client\" />\n</Cards>\n\nIntegrations [#integrations]\n\nAn issued identity needs a consumer that trusts its issuer, validates the certificate and grants the device permissions. Prepare both the device's trust in the server and the server's trust in the device.\n\nThe [AWS IoT Core guide](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core) explains how to use the identity in that destination. Provisioning in Lamassu and provisioning in the destination are separate decisions; review the conditions of the chosen mode before expecting state synchronization.\n\nWho prepares each part [#who-prepares-each-part]\n\n| Participant                | Responsibility                                                           |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| PKI administrator          | CA, issuance profile, chain and revocation publication.                  |\n| Provisioning administrator | DMS, admission, authentication per operation and inventory.              |\n| Device integrator          | Initial credential, key, EST client, trust and certificate installation. |\n| Consumer integrator        | Trusted issuers, validation and device permissions in the destination.   |\n\n[Permissions](/docs/platform/administration/access-control) and [audit](/docs/platform/administration/audit-logs) are shared with the rest of Platform. Prepare installation and instance connectivity in [Deployment](/docs/deployment/overview).\n"]
